hasher: hash transfers in-stream even when the source has the hashes

wrapInHashingReader (Fs.Put, Object.Update) skipped hashing the stream
when the source supplied every kept hash type (e.g. S3 with
--hasher-hashes=md5) and cached the source's sums instead. The
destination's Hash() then returned the source value, so the
post-transfer check compared the source hash with itself and missed
corruption in transit, which got cached under the source's hash.

Always hash the stream; fall back to the source's sums only when the
hashing reader cannot be created.

